A still moment — no weather, no tide, no wind, nothing moving anywhere. The world holding its breath. It does this, rarely, and no one knows for what.
[Across the fringe, vast and unhurried, a Greenwatcher passes. It is carrying something asleep, and carrying it gently, the way you carry a thing to bed. It does not look at you.]
It plants itself between the marsh and the worst of it, glowing, patient. Some creatures don't fight. They attend.
[It tucks its sleeping burden into the loam, petal by careful petal, and moves on. Enjoy the quiet. Distrust it. Both.]
